 all but won the AFC South what do we  make of the Titans at this point you  know they are the ultimate  jekyll-and-hyde team this year they beat  the Cowboys on a Monday night they  trounced the Patriots by 24 then they  lose by 28 to the Colts and then they're  back on Monday night and they lose by 17  in Houston which Titans team is the real  Titans team you know to me the Titans  shining moment this year so far was when  they went to Dallas and won on Monday  night a couple of weeks ago and the  reason why that was such an impressive  victory for that team is that if you  look at what Dallas does well Dallas  runs the ball well and not a lot of  teams can defend the Dallas running game  and I think that night what my Treville  said was we are going to be tough and we  are going to beat this team with  physicality that's what they did in that  game Mike I think the one other thing  about Tennessee right now is and the  reason why I don't think it's over but I  think it's going to be really really  hard for them is that I really wonder  right now is there anything that they  absolutely can hang their hat on that  they do offensively and I know Mariota  had this great 22 out of 23 game last  night that's great okay but I just don't  see the consistency on offense and look  at look at this scoring graphic right  now I just don't see the consistency on  offense that you need to have to be a  very good team and a playoff team you  know I always say there's three types of  teams in the NFL teams that have  franchise quarterbacks teams that are  looking for franchise quarterbacks and  then the teams that have a quarterback  and they're not quite sure whether or  not he's gonna be a franchise  quarterback this is your four for Marcus  Mariota he's not a franchise quarterback  yet he's not a bust he's somewhere in  that that middle ground and at what  point do you say he just is who he is  and we're either happy with that or  we're gonna try to upgrade when all  these oth